WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:06.980
ISIS just claimed a major new terror attack in the Belgian capital of Brussels

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.400
to understand why they would do this, you have to look at something that changed for ISIS about a year ago

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.300
and pretty far away in the middle east

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.380
So ISIS in the summer of 2014

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.260
had had a huge sweep across the region, seizing lots of cities

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.180
Starting in early 2015, the group began to suffer some real defeats in Syria and Iraq

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:36.460
lost some major cities and started to come under attack from American airstrikes

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.260
and in just a few months it lost a quarter of its territory

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.400
but this posed more than just a military threat to ISIS

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.120
It had always operated on a narrative of victory and invinsibility

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.920
and it used that to recruit and motivate fighters of other Jihadist groups

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.420
and it needs those fighters to survive

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.460
the was caliphate was losing ground so it was losing that narrative

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.740
and it needed something new to keep that going so

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.980
first they tried to expand abroad, Libya, Afghanistan, Yemen

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:06.860
but those efforts all fizzled, in the summer and fall of 2015

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:12.000
ISIS found its solution, by launching mass terror attacks against civilians abroad

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:17.560
and this helped the group portray itself once again as on the march

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.340
but then Europe faced a big problem in how to deal with these attacks

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:27.280
because the hard truth is that most of these attackers aren't foreigners. They aren't refugees or migrants

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:29.220
they're actually European nationals

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.040
and you can't just close the border to keep them out if they're actually from Europe

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:40.080
and a lot of them are people who went and joined ISIS or other terrorist groups, so-called foreign fighters

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.060
and now that ISIS is losing territory, those fighters are coming home, and they're bringing

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:47.680
their battled hardened experience and skills with them

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:53.000
and these are really hard problems to solve, rooted in socio-economic problems

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:56.500
grievances that go pretty deep in European society

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.840
you can't solve this with bombs or with border closings

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:00.780
So what now?

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.460
It seems likely that as ISIS keeps losing its territory

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:11.200
its going to become something like what it was before, when America was fighting the Iraq war in the mid 2000's

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:14.760
Not a state, but still an insurgency and a terrorist group

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.860
capable of doing terrible damage abroad.

